# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Line-ending policy
#
#  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#  Git's `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and what this machine has)
#  stores files as LF in the repository but converts them to CRLF on checkout.
#  That is invisible almost everywhere — except in one place where it broke a
#  real tool:
#
#      `npm run sync-migrations -- --check` builds each expected migration in
#      memory with '\n'.join() and byte-compares it against the file on disk.
#      With autocrlf the disk copy has CRLF headers, so the comparison could
#      NEVER match: the check reported all 7 migrations "stale" on a repo that
#      was perfectly in sync. Verified: the SQL bodies were byte-identical and
#      only the generated header differed.
#
#  Worse, "fixing" it by re-running the generator wrote LF headers next to
#  CRLF bodies, turning a false alarm into 7 genuinely modified files.
#
#  THE FIX: pin the file types where line endings are load-bearing to LF, so
#  the bytes on disk match the bytes in git and the drift check is meaningful.
#  Deliberately NOT a blanket `* text=auto` — this repo commits node_modules
#  and vendored third-party trees (Interstellar, scramjet, DayDream, NautilusOS),
#  and renormalizing those would rewrite thousands of files nobody here owns.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# SQL — the schema. sync-migrations byte-compares these, so LF is required for
# `--check` to work at all. Covers db/ (source of truth) and supabase/migrations.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Python — all 5 tools/*.py carry a `#!/usr/bin/env python3` shebang. A CRLF
# shebang makes Linux report "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env python3\r".
# (Currently LF in git, so this pins existing-correct behavior rather than
# changing it — it stops a future Windows-side edit from committing CRLF.)
*.py text eol=lf

# Shell scripts — same shebang hazard, and CRLF breaks `sh` parsing outright.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Server + tooling JavaScript. Node tolerates CRLF, so this is about keeping
# diffs clean rather than correctness.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js  text eol=lf

# Config / docs where a stray ^M shows up in diffs and terminal output.
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Dockerfile is consumed by a Linux builder.
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# ── Binary: never touch, never diff, never renormalize ─────────────────────
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.exe  binary
*.wasm binary
*.csv  binary

# ── Vendored third-party trees: leave exactly as upstream shipped them ──────
# These are reference/companion apps, not ZoFHub source. Renormalizing them
# would produce enormous diffs in code this project does not maintain.
Interstellar/** -text
scramjet/**     -text
DayDream/**     -text
NautilusOS/**   -text
node_modules/** -text
